  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Like terms must have the same variables, with matching exponents for each variable. The terms \\(3ab\\) and \\(-ba\\) have the same variables, all with exponent 1 (the order of the variables does not matter), so they are like terms; the other pairs have different variables or exponents.",
